// What swag is told to describe differently from what the Go type says. It is
// read by `make openapi`; see the target in the Makefile.

// textCode names a string the server sends that is not a refusal. Described as
// itself it becomes an enumeration of every code, and the order swag writes
// those in is not stable: the constants are declared beside the handler that
// sends each one, across several files, and the file order swag collects them
// in changes from run to run. The generated file is committed, so that shows up
// as a diff nobody made, five runs of the generator producing three different
// files.
//
// errorCode is left alone on purpose. Its constants are all in one block in
// internal/api/errors.go, so its order is settled by the source, and it is the
// list worth having in the description: error_code is what a script matches a
// refusal on.
replace github.com/jollaman999/tunnel-manager/internal/api.textCode string
